     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><div xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\"><hr/><p><b>English</b></p><hr/><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: CodeSystem KGL3Predicates</b></p><a name=\"KGL3Predicates\"> </a><a name=\"hcKGL3Predicates\"> </a><p>This case-sensitive code system <code>http://smart.who.int/base/CodeSystem/KGL3Predicates</code> defines the following codes:</p><table class=\"codes\"><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">implementedBy<a name=\"KGL3Predicates-implementedBy\"> </a></td><td>An L2 component is implemented by a FHIR artefact. Reused from l1 and licensed here per (component, resource) pair transcribed from the published mapping table. ALWAYS `inferred`, never `derived`: with no back-pointer extension in the estate, the join is a naming convention or a canonical reference, and every instance records which rule matched and a resolutionStatus. The optional `targetPath` property on an instance names the element reached (e.g. `PlanDefinition.action[2]`) so traceability can be element-level without this layer modelling FHIR internals as nodes.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">citesSource<a name=\"KGL3Predicates-citesSource\"> </a></td><td>A FHIR artefact cites an L1 source through `relatedArtifact[type = #citation]`. The target is an l1:citation minted from the same string by tools/extract-citations.mjs, so L3 and L1 join without either extractor knowing about the other -- the same mechanism l2-dmn uses from a decision rule.</td></tr><tr><td style=\"white-space:nowrap\">uses<a name=\"KGL3Predicates-uses\"> </a></td><td>One FHIR artefact references another by canonical: a PlanDefinition its Library, an action its ActivityDefinition, a Questionnaire its StructureMap, a Measure its Library. These are real canonical references rather than conventions, so unlike implementedBy they are `derived` when read straight from the